# A3 links "most sacred part of all morality" (justice grounded on utility) to mankind's belief that justice is "more sacred than policy".
# One could suspect that the common belief takes "sacred" as independent of utility, while Mill takes it as more binding within utility.
# But both statements read "sacred" as "more binding", and policy here means mere expediency. So I read A3 as joining two different claims, not as a bridge.
